@startuml
title Retry and deterministic backoff for one activity effect
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Executing\n(attempt a)" as Executing #E9F5EA
state "Routed onward\n(disposition completed)" as Routed #D9EFDF
state "Retry wait\nretry:{token}:{a+1}" as RetryWait #FFF0D9
state "Routed by failure disposition\n(failed / timedOut / resourceExhausted / custom)" as FailureRoute #F8DADA

[*] --> Executing : effect requested\n(effectRequested)
Executing --> Routed : observation completed\n/ push compensation record if declared
Executing --> RetryWait : retryable disposition\n[<latex>a < \mathrm{maxAttempts}</latex>]\n/ attempt := a + 1, retryScheduled
RetryWait --> Executing : timerFired [exact deadline]\nor retry command\n(Enter phase: the node re-executes)
Executing --> FailureRoute : retryable disposition\n[<latex>a = \mathrm{maxAttempts}</latex>]\nor non-retryable disposition
Routed --> [*]
FailureRoute --> [*] : routes like any trigger\n(retry budgets never mask outcomes)

note right of RetryWait #EAF7EE
Deterministic schedule, normative in the specification:
<latex>d_a = \min\!\bigl(d_{\max},\; d_0 \cdot (m/1000)^{\,a-2}\bigr)</latex>
With deterministic jitter enabled the delay is REPLACED
by a uniform deterministic sample from <latex>[0, d_a]</latex>:
<latex>\mathrm{SHA256}(k \,\Vert\, \texttt{":"} \,\Vert\, a)[0..8] \bmod (d_a + 1)</latex>
where <latex>k</latex> is the effect key, so replay and
recovery compute identical deadlines.
end note
note bottom of Executing #FFF3C9
Retryable means: the disposition is in the node's
retryOn list, or the list is empty and the disposition
is failed, timedOut, or resourceExhausted.
end note
@enduml
